  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Findings, cell 14** ([2,1,0]², point 1, 2026-09-27). Question: does adding a $k_2^2$ term at $\\theta_1+2h$ to $\\langle k_2^{u/h}Q_{12}\\rangle$ still give a product overlap $\\langle v\\otimes\\mathrm{vacL}|\\Psi_A\\rangle$?\n\n- **With $Q_{12}$: trivially yes.** $Q_{12}(\\theta_1+2h)=0$ for all 64 states, because of the factor $F=\\nu_1$ (cell 13). The term adds nothing.\n- **With $Q^3$ (the factor stripped): no.** $\\langle k_1Q_1\\rangle\\cdot Q^3(\\theta_1+2h)/N$ is not in the 8-dim product span. Relative residuals are $0.59$ ($k_1^0$) and $0.057$ ($k_1^1$) for $N=Q^3(\\theta_1)$, and $0.070$ and $0.14$ for $N=Q^3(\\theta_1+h)$. This stays true even if any admixture of the other two $Q^3$ values is allowed ($0.59$, $0.068$ at $k_1^0$).\n- **Sanity check.** $Q_{12}(\\theta_1+h)$ and $Q^3(\\theta_1+h)$ are in the span to $10^{-80}$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  }
